        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T15:01:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I spent three days attempting to see if Chrome, Android, and G3 could be moved to SkPathBuilder by adding things missing to SkPathBuilder. The answer is absolutely not. It would be required to make SkPathBuilder exactly the same as SkPath for at least some period of time in order to do the migration without being able to do an enormous all-at-once change across all the repos. There is no means to incrementally move to the current SkPathBuilder.",
      "parentUuid": "9e2afd6c_6b7beaab",
      "revId": "630ab5e7f877b15e29684549c24d2a553038f6a4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41c1300c_d73c7877",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T15:09:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you share some of the issues you ran into?  I might have been lucky, but converting canvas to SkPathBuilder was manageable (passing tests): https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/5906078\n\nWe can expand SkPathBuilder as needed, as long as the additions are *builder* related.\n\nThe problem I have with aliasing SkPath is that it\u0027s not a real migration: I can change the first spot I find in chromium, and call it a day - things will build and work fine.  Without the compiler enforcing the distinction, there is nothing to guide the refactoring or verify that we are indeed done.  Then you run into the exact same issues, just at a later time.",
      "parentUuid": "4291c5ca_4ab2fd29",
      "revId": "630ab5e7f877b15e29684549c24d2a553038f6a4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "be43e904_887e970c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T16:04:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And migrating to SkPathBuilder also isn\u0027t a migration, because there is no immutable SkPath so it doesn\u0027t matter because you haven\u0027t caught where the mutations happen. And in the process we now have two builders. Removing the existing SkPathBuilder, re-naming the existing SkPath as SkPathBuilder with an alias to SkPath, with a new immutable interface SkPath available with a build flag (for finding where SkPath is being used mutably) is the only real way forward.\n\nSo far I\u0027ve been defensive here. However, I do believe that doing this CL is a huge net negative for Skia as a whole. I would need overwhelming evidence that this approach can actually be made to work across all users and allow them a migration path this isn\u0027t an immediate all-or-nothing. And this really does mean all users and not just a little bit here or there.",
      "parentUuid": "41c1300c_d73c7877",
      "revId": "630ab5e7f877b15e29684549c24d2a553038f6a4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25f0a13c_d37bc12c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T17:34:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Whatever you think makes the current approach difficult (I have asked repeatedly for concrete examples, asking one more time) *is* the migration.  You can kick it down the road by continuing to use SkPath as a builder, but when we\u0027re done renaming and it\u0027s time to actually scrub the API we\u0027ll have to go back and fix the exact same things that we would be fixing incrementally as part of the SkPathBuilder conversion.\n\n\n\u003e I would need overwhelming evidence\n\nSure, I am willing to work on providing that evidence by actually migrating clients using the current pattern.  There little to no risk: if things don\u0027t work out, we can delete the current builder impl and alias SkPath.  We\u0027d still be in better shape with some clients already converted.\n\n\n\u003e allow them a migration path this isn\u0027t an immediate all-or-nothing\n\nI must be missing something, because SkPathBuilder absolutely offers an incremental migration path.",
      "parentUuid": "be43e904_887e970c",
      "revId": "630ab5e7f877b15e29684549c24d2a553038f6a4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
